Z||000000||87FieroGT||05-06-2000||01:03 AM||||Well I am finally starting to repaint my Fiero and boy what a job it is. It thought sanding down all the parts was the hard part but I was wrong. I started shooting it last night but then ran into some problems. I noticed that the paint looked really rough so I stopped for the night since it was getting late. I went back to the paint store to show the guy I bought the paint from what was happening. He said if I could wait a few minutes he would come over to the house and give me some tips since he paints cars on the side as well. He made it look so easy, but I learn very easy from watching someone do something rather than read about it. <BR>    Anyway I went back and reshot the peices I was working with and then did the clear coat. It looks emaculate. I still have most of the other body panels to do since I only left the rear clip and the roof panel on the car. The rest should go a lot faster since I made all the mistakes already. I will post some pics as soon I am done. By the way those of you who had seen my car before with the Konig Rush rims would know that it was blue but I found from working on the car that some of the panels were replaced on the drivers side with red panels that were painted over and by looking at the other side the paint was not the true 87 blue color. So I made the decision to go with a color I think looks good on a sporty car. It it a custom yellow and should be seen a couple miles away. I can't wait to get those pics on here.||||reg||10
